---
description: Routes every request to the repo's canonical agent instructions and working journal
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before working. It is the canonical instruction file for
all AI tools here and points to the design document and the journal.

Two things it will tell you that are worth knowing up front:

- `docs/journal/` records beliefs this project held and then disproved. Run
  `grep -rn "Previously believed" docs/journal/` before making a design decision, changing a
  dependency version, or debugging something that "should work."
- Write a journal entry before finishing a session in which a belief changed, a non-obvious
  fact was learned, or a claim you made turned out wrong. Format is in
  `docs/journal/GUIDELINES.md`.

This rule is deliberately a pointer and holds no rules of its own, so it cannot drift out of
step with `AGENTS.md`. Put substance there. Add further `.mdc` files here only for rules
genuinely scoped to a path via `globs`.
